# ML artefacts.
#
# The serving set is COMMITTED on purpose — about 1.5 MB total. A cloud deploy
# builds from a git clone, so if the models were not in the repo the API would
# start, fail to load a bundle, and crash on the first request. Committing them
# is what makes `git push` -> deploy actually work without a separate artefact
# store. They are also what lets a reviewer clone the repo and get a running
# service without a 10-minute training run first.
#
# Excluded are the two files that are large and only needed for the local demo
# and drift baseline, both regenerated by `python -m argus_ml.train`.
ml/artifacts/recent_transactions.parquet
ml/artifacts/reference_sample.parquet
ml/artifacts_smoke/
mlruns/

